tags: inter_affairs

= Securing Class-Ds

Regardless of violating ethics and basic human rights, The site has no choice but to use Class-D personnel whether for tests or other activities. How should we secure Class-Ds?

- @inmate: Death row inmates, our usual approach.
- @criminals: Criminals convicted of serious crimes.
- @nhi: NHIs, homeless, drug addicts and other expendable civilians.
- @root: We either don't want to or cannot secure D-Classes right now.
- @easy_discard

@inmate
subtitle: -2 resources
choose-if: resources >= 2 and inmate_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources <= 1 : Not enough resources. ?][? if inmate_timer >= 1 : There are currently no death row inmates we could secure. ?]
on-arrival: resources -= 2; inmate_timer += 2; class_d += 10; class_d_strength += 5; class_d_riot += 2; exposure += 1

We have secured inmates convicted of crimes punishable by death as Class-D personnels from various high security prisons.

@criminals
subtitle: -2 resources
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; class_d += 20; class_d_strength += 5; class_d_riot += 5; exposure += 2; ethics_commitee_relation -= 3

We have secured criminals convited of serious crimes as Class-D personnels from various prisons.

@nhi
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; class_d += 15; class_d_riot += 1; exposure += 5; ethics_commitee_relation -= 10; ethics_commitee_relation -= 5 if resources <= 1; ethics_commitee_relation += 3 if inmate_timer >= 1

We have activated protocol 12 to secure NHIs as Class-D personnels. Whether we did or did not do this in time of duress, the Ethics Committee are displeased and reviewing our actions.
